{"schemaVersion":1,"workId":"OL86343W","title":"A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man","authors":["James Joyce","James Joyce","james joyce"],"firstPublished":1818,"edition":{"description":"Sections as detected in Project Gutenberg eBook #4217.","source":"Project Gutenberg eBook #4217","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4217"},"sectionLabel":{"singular":"Chapter","plural":"Chapters"},"sections":[{"id":"s1","label":"Ch. 1"},{"id":"s2","label":"Ch. 2"},{"id":"s3","label":"Ch. 3"},{"id":"s4","label":"Ch. 4"},{"id":"s5","label":"Ch. 5"}],"groups":[{"id":"g-dedalus","label":"Dedalus (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"stephen-dedalus","name":"Stephen Dedalus","aliases":["Stephen"],"role":"protagonist","group":"g-dedalus","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “—O, Stephen will apologise.”"},{"id":"cranly","name":"Cranly","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Why was it that when he thought of Cranly he could never raise before his mind the entire image of his body but only the image of the head and face?”"},{"id":"mr-dedalus","name":"Mr. Dedalus","aliases":["Dedalus"],"role":"major","group":"g-dedalus","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “—Tell us, Dedalus, do you kiss your mother before you go to bed?”"},{"id":"temple","name":"Temple","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “—Go on, Temple, said a stout ruddy student near him.”"},{"id":"lynch","name":"Lynch","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “—Lynch is awake, said Cranly.”"},{"id":"dante","name":"Dante","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Uncle Charles and Dante clapped.”"},{"id":"mr-casey","name":"Mr. Casey","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “There were two sides in it: Dante was on one side and his father and Mr Casey were on the other side but his mother and uncle Charles were on no side.”"},{"id":"heron","name":"Heron","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Two boys were standing in the shelter of a doorway, smoking, and before he reached them he had recognised Heron by his voice.”"},{"id":"fleming","name":"Fleming","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “He drank another cup of hot tea and Fleming said:”"},{"id":"charles","name":"Charles","aliases":["Uncle Charles"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Uncle Charles and Dante clapped.”"},{"id":"davin","name":"Davin","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “It was a Firbolg in the borrowed cloak of a Milesian; and he thought of his friend Davin, the peasant student.”"},{"id":"simon-moonan","name":"Simon Moonan","aliases":["Simon"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Simon Moonan told him not to because the prefect was looking.”"},{"id":"father-arnall","name":"Father Arnall","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Father Arnall knew more than Dante because he was a priest but both his father and uncle Charles said that Dante was a clever woman and a wellread woman.”"},{"id":"wells","name":"Wells","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “That was mean of Wells to shoulder him into the square ditch because he would not swop his little snuffbox for Wells’s seasoned hacking chestnut, the conqueror of forty.”"},{"id":"dixon","name":"Dixon","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “—We had better go, Dixon, said Stephen in warning.”"},{"id":"brother-michael","name":"Brother Michael","aliases":["Michael"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “—We must pack off to Brother Michael because we have the collywobbles!”"},{"id":"athy","name":"Athy","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “He told Stephen that his name was Athy and that his father kept a lot of racehorses that were spiffing jumpers and that his father would give a good tip to Brother Michael any time he wanted it because Brother Michael…”"},{"id":"father-dolan","name":"Father Dolan","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Father Dolan will be in to see you every day.”"},{"id":"john","name":"John","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “O, we had a good walk, hadn’t we, John?”"},{"id":"mrs-dedalus","name":"Mrs. Dedalus","role":"minor","group":"g-dedalus","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Mrs Dedalus followed and the places were arranged.”"},{"id":"parnell","name":"Parnell","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “The brush with the maroon velvet back was for Michael Davitt and the brush with the green velvet back was for Parnell.”"},{"id":"stevie","name":"Stevie","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “—Go on, Stevie, I have a hard head, you tell me.”"},{"id":"moynihan","name":"Moynihan","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Stephen glanced up quickly but Moynihan’s snoutish face, outlined on the grey light, was impassive.”"},{"id":"mary","name":"Mary","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “—Mary?”"},{"id":"boland","name":"Boland","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Boland, his friend, marched beside him, a large grin on his face, while Nash came on a few steps behind, blowing from the pace and wagging his great red head.”"},{"id":"aquinas","name":"Aquinas","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “His mind when wearied of its search for the essence of beauty amid the spectral words of Aristotle or Aquinas turned often for its pleasure to the dainty songs of the Elizabethans.”"},{"id":"nash","name":"Nash","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Boland, his friend, marched beside him, a large grin on his face, while Nash came on a few steps behind, blowing from the pace and wagging his great red head.”"},{"id":"glynn","name":"Glynn","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “—Goggins was waiting for you, Glynn.”"},{"id":"nasty-roche","name":"Nasty Roche","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Rody Kickham was a decent fellow but Nasty Roche was a stink.”"},{"id":"cecil-thunder","name":"Cecil Thunder","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “—I know why, Cecil Thunder said.”"},{"id":"francis-xavier","name":"Francis Xavier","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “But he thought they were the portraits of the saints and great men of the order who were looking down on him silently as he passed: saint Ignatius Loyola holding an open book and pointing to the words _Ad Majorem Dei…”"},{"id":"eileen","name":"Eileen","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “They were Eileen’s father and mother.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"charles","target":"dante","weight":10,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":10,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r2","source":"charles","target":"parnell","weight":3,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":3,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r3","source":"dante","target":"parnell","weight":12,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":10,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":12}]},{"id":"r4","source":"dante","target":"eileen","weight":3,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":3,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r5","source":"eileen","target":"parnell","weight":3,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":3,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r6","source":"eileen","target":"stephe